# CHEM-WIRE — chemistry conditioning integration (2026-09-03)

Status: WIRED, toggle ON. [CLAUDE] drafted, [NICHOLAS] approved wiring.
Companion engine + tests live in `mathjax-intent-extension` (000-BBB).

## What this adds
Two pieces from the intent extension, for the HTML/EPUB output path only:
1. **chemmark** (MathJax TeX package, inside the bundle): stamps
   `data-chem` markers on everything `\ce{...}` emits during typesetting,
   so downstream code knows which MathML came from chemistry.
2. **chemConditionDocument** (exported by the bundle): post-pass over the
   serialized MathML that (a) PRE-SPLITS compact formulas so MathCAT's
   token splitter cannot drop atoms (upstream bug R1: "concentration of
   cap H" losing the Cl), and (b) STAMPS `:chemical-formula` intent
   properties on marked spans so MathCAT treats them as chemistry even
   where its own detection would fail or veto.

