## Route note
Conditioning runs only where the device transform runs: the baked-MathML
route (tex2mml in-browser at CONVERSION time). The MathJax-mode route
(raw TeX shipped to the reader's page, client-side typeset via the Lua
filter's inline extension) has no conditioning hook, so chem pages meant
for MathCAT/SRE should be produced via the baked route. Extending
chemmark to the inline extension is possible but pointless without a
client-side conditioning pass — noted as future work, not a gap in this
wiring.
